{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED for exact clean head 7db213dfd5b86ada60c0fb1ec3914b111dcb857a, naming the primary docs artifact c741f291af46bf3d1a267b10c1b056b6ed03debc at path `docs`.\n\nHead is a clean fast-forward from main a3d097dd: 21 files, +238/-113, docs and SKILL.md plus internal/docset/citation_baseline.txt. I reviewed the main...head diff at that exact commit, not any intermediate or parallel head.\n\nWHAT I RAN, not read. `make vet` 0, `make build` 0, `make test` 0 — 19 packages ok, internal/docset 111.5s, no FAIL and no failure lines. Because `go test` prints no skip without -v, and the basis gate is built to skip when it finds no workroom, I re-ran it verbosely: TestGateEveryNamedActResolvesToALiveRecord and TestGateEveryPageNamesAGoverningAct both PASS, not SKIP. The citations were genuinely resolved against the real record.\n\nCONDITIONS.\n- Monotonic baseline: 32 entries to 19, and set difference confirms no event was added. Several surviving entries also lost pages, which is the page-set mechanism recording real re-anchoring rather than a flat count.\n- No page this head touched still carries baseline debt: the intersection of the 21 changed paths with the pages named in the head's baseline is empty.\n- Non-self-referential: no page rests on an artifact whose commit is this head.\n- All nine artifacts cited by docs/README.md and docs/anchoring.md resolve, are live and are non-stale, against the fold's own retirement signal.\n- Fan-out: each of the five gate artifacts governs 2 pages, far under the gate's len(pages)/4 limit, and the flare gate enforces it.\n- Eleven-tool map: the shipping server registers exactly ack, inspect, presence, ratify, say, state, status, supersede, wait, whoami, work; eleven pages exist and README lists eleven. The surface gate reads this from source, so it cannot drift silently.\n- Four gates, five test files, and the table is truthful: \"no empty basis\" spans basis_test.go and anchor_test.go.\n\nARCHITECTURE. Affected