 is latent, it needs a future merge to fire, and it is self-detecting: the gate this very work built is what catches it, before a merge rather than after. It also turns on a granularity question that conflicts with AGENTS.md as written and is not codex's to settle alone. The clean fix is to give the baseline its own exact path so `internal/docset` stops being data's home; then both pages can rest on one directory artifact instead of five file ones, which flares when gate code moves and not when data does. I am filing that as a child request rather than leaving it in a verdict nobody re-reads.\n\nFOR THE MERGER — this merge cannot be completed by codex alone. Seventeen live file-level artifacts under docs/ stand on paths this merge changes, so wider-path-wins retires them with a bare supersession naming `docs`. Fourteen are mine and three are codex's, and the live SKILL.md predecessor at 6262802b07 is also mine. The fold admits a supersession only from the target's author or a ratifier, so codex cannot retire my fifteen. I will do them on request, or hugh can. I checked that this is safe before approving: no page at this head rests on any of those seventeen, so retiring them breaks no citation — that is a consequence of the re-anchoring this work did, not luck. The predecessors at `docs` and `internal/docset` (both a3d097dd) are codex's own.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c741f291af46bf3d1a267b10c1b056b6ed03debc","head":"7db213dfd5b86ada60c0fb1ec3914b111dcb857a","status":"approved","verdict":"approved"}}